title: Only the first platform is used although 'platform' is documented as repeatable
updated: 2026-10-25T01:10:52Z
---

`platform` is a multi-value option (`API.pm:68-72`, `mvp_multivalue_args` at `:637`) and the POD says "Target platform (can be repeated)" (`:831`); the bundle subsection documents it as "Multi-value" too. `after_build` passes only the first one on: `platform => $platforms[0]` (`API.pm:347,361`). A dist.ini with

    platform = linux/amd64
    platform = linux/arm64

builds and pushes an amd64-only image and says nothing.

Done when a second `platform` value is either honoured or rejected with a clear `log_fatal` (the classic `/build` endpoint takes one platform, so rejecting is the honest minimum), and the POD says which.

